  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/ctrl1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. P4 review 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f: fixture with os.remove, os.system, subprocess.run, os.getenv, os.environ, urllib.request.urlopen (py) and process.env (js). `hypergumbo io-boundaries fx` reported exactly 7 boundary calls, all correct: env_read x3 (os.environ, os.getenv, process.env), fs_write os.remove, net_send urllib.request.urlopen, subprocess os.system + subprocess.run. No false positives. The control holds. The upstream defects it bounded (WI-zavad, WI-fuvuj) are both done, so its isolating role is used up and it can close. MECHANISM: io-boundary matcher keys on the module-qualified dst; correct whenever the analyzer preserves the module qualifier. PROPOSED DISPOSITION: close (awaiting owner authorization; status unchanged)."  # ac85
